description:
Design a two-input AND gate using NOR gates. The circuit utilizes two NOR gates to create inverters for the inputs A and B, then connects these outputs to a third NOR gate to produce the AND functionality. When both A and B are HIGH, the output Y will also be HIGH; otherwise, Y will be LOW.
module top_module(
    input A,
    input B,
    output Y
);

code:
module top_module(
    input A,
    input B,
    output Y
);wire notA, notB, nor_out;

    // Implementing NOT using NOR gate
    assign notA = ~(A | A); // Equivalent to NOT A
    assign notB = ~(B | B); // Equivalent to NOT B

    // Implementing AND using NOR gates
    assign nor_out = ~(notA | notB); // NOR of notA and notB
    assign Y = nor_out; // Output Y is connected to the NOR gate result

endmodule

