description:
Design a circuit that implements a 2-input Muller gate with an active-low reset. When the reset (rstn) is low, the output (z) is set to low. If the reset is high and the inputs (a and b) are equal, the output (z) is assigned the value of either input after a one-time unit delay. This module essentially behaves like a conditional buffer that maintains its output when inputs match, but resets under the specified condition.
module top_module(

   z,

   a, b, rstn
   );

code:
module top_module(

   z,

   a, b, rstn
   );input  a;
  input  b;
  input  rstn;
  output z;



  reg                   z;


  always @* begin
    if(rstn == 1'b0) begin
      z <= 0;
    end
    else begin
      if(a == b)
        z <= #1 a;
    end

  end



endmodule

